error[NK1306]: `mut` here marks an element of a set, and a set's element can't be changed in place.
  --> tests/a_for_mut_over_a_set_is_refused.nika:6:9
   |
 6 |     for mut s in seen {
   |         ^^^ marks a set's element
   |
   = note: An element decides where it stands in the set (its order, or its hash), so one changed in place would stand in the wrong place.
   = help: Take the element out of the set and insert the changed one after the loop.
